('The description asks for a supported historical/economic judgment about dyes and the chemical industry. DE/EN agree and the page leaves room for competing causes.', '43a2f7b0', 'The BY economic significance component fits. Employment/output data alone do not establish general welfare or isolate industrial causality.', 'Die lernende Person erklärt bei neuen Branchenanteilen die begrenzte Aussage von Umsätzen und berücksichtigt konkurrierende Ursachen.', 'With changed sector shares, the learner explains the limited meaning of revenues and considers competing causes.', 'The fictional 200→600 employees, 20→120 t output, price 12→5 and research 4→30 provide assessable relationships. Railway expansion is a confounder. Dye share 70→35 is −35 percentage points; constant total revenue does not establish overall profitability or welfare without costs and other data.'),
('The goal connects acid/base or redox structural change to indicator colour. The bilingual body and page distinguish changed species from resonance contributors.', '4ac0512a', 'The BY acid/base-redox indicator component fits. A colour change alone is not a calibrated pH measurement.', 'Die lernende Person deutet bei neuer pH-Lage oder Luftoxidation geänderte Teilchenspezies und begrenzt daraus abgeleitete Messwerte.', 'For changed pH or air oxidation, the learner interprets changed species and bounds inferred measured values.', 'At pKa 7, pH 6/8 gives base/acid ratios 0.1/10. HIn and In− are distinct species, not contributors. B++H++2e−⇌BH balances charge; absorption at 530–700 nm leaves blue 430–480 nm in the simplified model. Reoxidation by air is not proof of a pH change.'),
('Halogenation and nitration are bounded examples of electrophilic aromatic substitution. DE/EN agree. The description does not require two unrelated complete syntheses; this remains distinct from the e594 finding.', 'he-chem-sekii-q2-3-b02,he-chem-sekii-q2-3-b04', 'HE names halogenation in the selected Q2.3 scope and nitration at LK. Nitration is not granted for HE GK by combining rows; catalyst/side-chain BY comparisons are separate components.', 'Die lernende Person begründet bei anderem Reagenz und Licht- oder Katalysatorbedingungen Ring- gegenüber Seitenkettenreaktion.', 'For changed reagent and light/catalyst conditions, the learner distinguishes ring from side-chain reaction.', 'Br2/FeBr3 formal electrophile bookkeeping is accepted without asserting freely solvated Br+. NO2+ ring attack shifts an N=O pair to avoid invalid nitrogen valence. Toluene under light gives radical side-chain reaction, distinct from catalysed ring substitution. No exact isomer yield is invented.'),
('The goal assesses the meaning and relative contributions of resonance structures. DE/EN and the native representation distinguish contributors from rearranged nuclei or distinct molecules.', 'ed3c553b,8cc77f16', 'The BY model-nature and energetic contributor components fit. Contributor energy is not the energy of independently observed exchanging benzene isomers.', 'Die lernende Person beurteilt eine neue ladungsgetrennte Grenzstruktur und grenzt Protonenverschiebung von Mesomerie ab.', 'The learner assesses a new charge-separated contributor and distinguishes proton relocation from resonance.', 'The supplied C1+ sextet/C2− lone-pair contributor conserves atoms and net zero charge but has lower weight than neutral contributors. Neutral symmetry-related contributors are equivalent. Moving H produces a changed nuclear arrangement and is not resonance.'),
('Acid/base comparisons are explicitly justified using inductive and mesomeric effects. DE/EN agree and the page links the particle model to stability rather than merely listing strength rankings.', 'ffc45d6f', 'The exact BY I/M acidity/basicity component fits; broader general acid/base rows do not automatically add all other comparisons.', 'Die lernende Person begründet bei größerem Substituentenabstand oder verändertem aromatischem Amin neue pKa-Vergleiche im gleichen Medium.', 'For increased substituent distance or a changed aromatic amine, the learner explains new pKa comparisons in the same medium.', 'Phenol pKa 10 versus ethanol 16 and anilinium 4.6 versus cyclohexylaminium 10.6 are interpreted within the same aqueous comparison. Chloroacetic 2.86 versus chloropropionic 4 and acetic 4.76 probe inductive distance. Nitro substitution lowers aniline N basicity; values are not transferred across solvents without qualification.'),
('The description asks for a substance-specific application and health judgment using chemical evidence and exposure. DE/EN agree. The native page does not turn the aromatic class into a common toxicity verdict.', 'e6a41254', 'The BY aromatic-use/health component fits. Individual product approval, personal cancer probability and all-aromatic hazard classification are outside this bounded review.', 'Die lernende Person vergleicht neue geschlossene oder offene Anwendungen und unterscheidet Gefahr von konkreter Exposition.', 'The learner compares changed closed or open uses and distinguishes hazard from actual exposure.', 'The benzene Group 1 statement is treated as hazard identification, not personal probability or a verdict for all aromatic substances. Closed process versus open cleaning changes exposure. Fictional volatile R versus dusty S requires route-specific information; no complete toxicity conclusion follows from volatility alone.'),
