('The sigma-complex formation and rearomatisation mechanism is explicit and assessable. DE/EN and the native scheme retain electron-pair movement, intermediate charge and proton loss.', 'he-chem-sekii-q2-3-b02,he-chem-sekii-q2-3-b04', 'Only the HE electrophilic-substitution mechanism components are assessed. Halogenation and LK nitration course restrictions remain separate.', 'Die lernende Person bilanziert in einem neuen σ-Komplex Bindungen, Ringladung und Deprotonierung mit einer passenden Base.', 'In a new sigma complex, the learner accounts for bonds, ring charge and deprotonation by a suitable base.', 'The attacked C1 has four bonds (H, electrophile and ring neighbours), with positive ring charge represented at C2/C4/C6. Rearomatisation removes H+, not hydride. Nitro N+/O− notation preserves octet; ring +1 and counterion bookkeeping conserve overall charge, with HSO4− giving H2SO4.')
